{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q424273","formula":"C₂H₃N","hill":"C2H3N","elements":["H","C","N"],"composition":{"C":2.0,"H":3.0,"N":1.0},"names":{"en":"2H-azirine","ru":"Азирин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Azirines are heterocyclic organic compounds containing a three-membered ring with two carbon atoms and one nitrogen atom, the unsaturated analogs of aziridines. Azirine, the parent compound, has two isomers: the antiaromatic 1H-azirine, containing a carbon–carbon double bond, is not stable and rearranges to the tautomeric 2H-azirine, containing a carbon–nitrogen double bond, which is at least 30 kcal·mol−1 lower in energy. 2H-Azirines can be considered strained imines and are isolable.","ru":"Азири́н (2H-азирин) — гетероциклическое соединение, трехчленный цикл с одной двойной связью и одним атомом азота. В свободном виде незамещенный не получен. Изомерен 1H-азирину."},"fame":15,"pubchemCid":135972,"mass":41.05,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1C=N1","inchikey":"NTJMGOWFGQXUDY-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2H-azirine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"135972","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.603,"y":0.525,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":0.875,"y":0.152,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.272,"y":-0.676,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":1.384,"y":0.355,"z":0.928,"el":"H"},{"x":1.383,"y":0.355,"z":-0.928,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.488,"y":-1.744,"z":0.0,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,2],[1,2,1],[1,3,1],[1,4,1],[2,5,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q424273","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azirine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%90%D0%B7%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%BD","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role"